                <pb facs="1023" n="899" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg899"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/160: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Mission at
                            Lausanne to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lausanne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-20T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 20,
                                1922—12 noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received November 20—10:18
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3. The selection of a permanent chairman seems to be a matter difficult to agree
                    upon, and it is said that the presidency will be offered to a representative of
                    the United States. We perceive no sufficient ground for acceptance unless the
                    Department believes there would be a positive increase in prestige or other
                    advantage. Immediate instructions requested.</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Child</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
